#{[17592186570038 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570038 #edb/ref 1069 "q-85376" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570038 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570038 #edb/ref 1071 "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{2}{1+\\sqrt{1-2w}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570038 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9419475-d219-538e-ac38-b80302aae79f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570038 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $1-\\sqrt{1-2w}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $1-\\sqrt{1-2w},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{1+\\sqrt{1-2w}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{1+\\sqrt{1-2w}}\\cdot \\frac{1-\\sqrt{1-2w}}{1-\\sqrt{1-2w}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(1-\\sqrt{1-2w})}{(1+\\sqrt{1-2w})(1-\\sqrt{1-2w})} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(1-\\sqrt{1-2w})}{{1}^{2}-(\\sqrt{1-2w})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(1-\\sqrt{1-2w})}{1-(1-2w)} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(1-\\sqrt{1-2w})}{2w} & = \\\\ \\frac{1-\\sqrt{1-2w}}{w}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570039 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570039 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34864" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570039 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570039 #edb/ref 1071 "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{m}{\\sqrt{m}+m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570039 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9d96fa3-8e95-5519-8ecc-c21bd99ca106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570039 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{m}-m.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{m}-m,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{m}{\\sqrt{m}+m} & = \\\\ \\frac{m}{\\sqrt{m}+m}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{m}-m}{\\sqrt{m}-m} & = \\\\ \\frac{m(\\sqrt{m}-m)}{(\\sqrt{m}+m)(\\sqrt{m}-m)} & = \\\\ \\frac{m(\\sqrt{m}-m)}{(\\sqrt{m})^{2}-{m}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{m(\\sqrt{m}-m)}{m-{m}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{m}(\\sqrt{m}-m)}{\\cancel{m}(1-m)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{m}-m}{1-m}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
